{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00193",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.3,
      "end_seconds": 7.63,
      "duration_seconds": 6.33,
      "text": "Doctor, your next patient is here. I've done the basics, I'll read them out in a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.06,
      "end_seconds": 12.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Thanks, that's helpful. Hello, please sit. What's been happening?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 13.41,
      "end_seconds": 15.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.78,
      "text": "It's sneezing fits, mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 15.65,
      "end_seconds": 17.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.85,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 18.3,
      "end_seconds": 20.34,
      "duration_seconds": 2.04,
      "text": "About... well, about a week."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 22.83,
      "end_seconds": 29.71,
      "duration_seconds": 6.88,
      "text": "Tell me a bit more about it: how bad it gets, how often, and whether anything makes it better or worse."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 31.13,
      "end_seconds": 41.93,
      "duration_seconds": 10.8,
      "text": "I notice it more with early mornings and dust. It happens on and off. Moderate, I'd say. I've had itchy watery eyes too, for three weeks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 43.48,
      "end_seconds": 47.14,
      "duration_seconds": 3.66,
      "text": "Do you have everything you need to get home alright?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 48.6,
      "end_seconds": 60.61,
      "duration_seconds": 12.01,
      "text": "Yes, I've got my transport sorted. It's a bit of a trek, but I'm used to the journey by now, and I brought something to read for the wait."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 61.13,
      "end_seconds": 64.72,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "Have you had any fever, facial pain or rash?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 65.3,
      "end_seconds": 66.95,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "No, none of those."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 67.75,
      "end_seconds": 70.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.07,
      "text": "Do you have any questions before we carry on?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 71.72,
      "end_seconds": 83.14,
      "duration_seconds": 11.42,
      "text": "Not at the moment, uh, I think you've covered most of what I was wondering. If something comes to mind later, I'll ask you before I leave."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 84.05,
      "end_seconds": 91.34,
      "duration_seconds": 7.29,
      "text": "Okay, so the vitals from earlier. Pulse 82, BP is 128 over 81, respiratory rate 14, SpO2 98 percent on room air."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 92.1,
      "end_seconds": 92.86,
      "duration_seconds": 0.76,
      "text": "Alright, thanks."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 93.61,
      "end_seconds": 96.42,
      "duration_seconds": 2.81,
      "text": "I want to open your previous notes quickly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.01,
      "end_seconds": 97.8,
      "duration_seconds": 0.79,
      "text": "Go ahead."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 111.79,
      "end_seconds": 119.47,
      "duration_seconds": 7.68,
      "text": "Okay, here we go. Any long-term health problems I should know about? I ask because it helps me narrow things down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 120.11,
      "end_seconds": 122.25,
      "duration_seconds": 2.14,
      "text": "Asthma, for about ten years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.2,
      "end_seconds": 135.56,
      "duration_seconds": 12.36,
      "text": "I like to make sure you understand what's happening, so please stop me at any point. There are no silly questions, and I'd much rather you ask now than go home still wondering about something."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 137.05,
      "end_seconds": 139.6,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Right, um, I understand now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.07,
      "end_seconds": 144.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.47,
      "text": "Do you drink alcohol?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 145.26,
      "end_seconds": 148.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.56,
      "text": "I have a couple of drinks on the weekend."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.04,
      "end_seconds": 152.36,
      "duration_seconds": 2.32,
      "text": "What medicines do you take regularly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.4,
      "end_seconds": 156.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.35,
      "text": "I take Asthalin inhaler, when needed for my asthma."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 157.09,
      "end_seconds": 159.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.7,
      "text": "Is the room warm enough for you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 161.03,
      "end_seconds": 163.79,
      "duration_seconds": 2.76,
      "text": "Um, it's perfect, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 164.17,
      "end_seconds": 168.22,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "What about family history, any illnesses that run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 168.67,
      "end_seconds": 170.19,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "My mother has diabetes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 170.67,
      "end_seconds": 173.99,
      "duration_seconds": 3.32,
      "text": "Do you need me to explain anything as we go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 175.38,
      "end_seconds": 181.31,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Just tell me in plain language, please. I'm not good with the medical terms."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 181.62,
      "end_seconds": 186.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.47,
      "text": "Any allergies I should know about? Just so I get the full picture."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 186.8,
      "end_seconds": 188.8,
      "duration_seconds": 2.0,
      "text": "No, nothing I'm aware of."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.2,
      "end_seconds": 193.92,
      "duration_seconds": 3.72,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.32,
      "end_seconds": 196.4,
      "duration_seconds": 2.08,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.94,
      "end_seconds": 206.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.51,
      "text": "Putting together what you've described, this looks most like allergic rhinitis. I want to be honest that this is an impression, not a final answer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.88,
      "end_seconds": 210.29,
      "duration_seconds": 2.41,
      "text": "Is this going to go away?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 210.89,
      "end_seconds": 228.1,
      "duration_seconds": 17.21,
      "text": "I understand the worry. At the moment I'd say it's allergic rhinitis, and we'll know more once the an allergy test is back. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had sneezing fits for about a week, moderate, and no rash or facial pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 229.58,
      "end_seconds": 231.01,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "That's it, yes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.09,
      "end_seconds": 247.07,
      "duration_seconds": 14.98,
      "text": "I'll be straight with you about how this works. Most of what we see in clinic turns out to be manageable, and the history you give me is often more useful than any single test, so thank you for being so detailed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.65,
      "end_seconds": 251.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.35,
      "text": "Thank you, that really helps."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 251.82,
      "end_seconds": 255.62,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an allergy test for allergic rhinitis."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 256.54,
      "end_seconds": 258.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Okay, you know, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 259.41,
      "end_seconds": 283.78,
      "duration_seconds": 24.37,
      "text": "I'd like you to take levocetirizine, 5 milligrams, at night, for two weeks. That should help with allergy symptoms. Keep the windows closed in the early morning and wash the bedsheets weekly in hot water. Make sure you're drinking plenty of fluids, two to three litres a day if you can, and get proper rest. If the symptoms get worse, or you feel really unwell, please don't wait, come to the emergency department."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 285.01,
      "end_seconds": 287.56,
      "duration_seconds": 2.55,
      "text": "Please come and see me in a month."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 289.15,
      "end_seconds": 293.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.25,
      "text": "Sure, you know, I'll make the appointment on the way out."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 296.65,
      "end_seconds": 304.13,
      "duration_seconds": 7.48,
      "text": "Just so I know I've explained it clearly, can you tell me the plan back in your own words?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.48,
      "end_seconds": 312.73,
      "duration_seconds": 8.25,
      "text": "So, I take the levocetirizine, 5 milligrams, at night and come back in a month. Is that right?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 316.17,
      "end_seconds": 320.56,
      "duration_seconds": 4.39,
      "text": "Alright, yes, exactly right. Okay, I think we're finished. Is everything clear?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 320.88,
      "end_seconds": 322.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.73,
      "text": "No questions. Thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 322.98,
      "end_seconds": 323.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.94,
      "text": "See you then."
    }
  ]
}